.TH SPRITEEDIT 1
.SH NAME
spriteedit \- edit TempleOS-style sprites embedded in text
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/spriteedit
[
.I file
[
.I name
]
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Spriteedit
is an Inferno RGBA sprite editor modelled on the TempleOS DolDoc sprite editor.
Its source format is an ordinary text block, so sprites can be kept inside
Limbo source, troff input, documentation, or a standalone asset file.
.PP
The block format is
.EX
.SPRITE cursor 2 2 r8g8b8a8
-16776961 -1
. 862388223
.ENDSPRITE
.EE
Pixels are signed 32-bit Inferno
.B r8g8b8a8
values separated by spaces.  A dot denotes a transparent pixel.  RGB sliders
and the r/R, g/G, and b/B keys edit the current full-colour paint value.
.PP
Mesh elements use the companion textual form
.EX
.MESH pyramid 4 2
v -20 -20 0
v 20 -20 0
v 20 20 0
v -20 20 0
f 12 0 1 2
f 12 0 2 3
.ENDMESH
.EE
where each face contains an Inferno RGBA value followed by three vertex
indices.  Mesh mode presents an editable orthographic view alongside a live
filled perspective preview.  Clicking selects a vertex, dragging moves it in
the current plane, and Tab cycles through XY, XZ, and ZY planes.  Space records
the selected vertex for a face, T creates a triangle from the last three
recorded vertices, and V creates a vertex at the origin.
.PP
If the named block already exists, saving replaces only that block and
preserves all surrounding text.  If it does not exist, a new block is
appended.  With no arguments the editor uses
.BR /tmp/sprite.txt
and the object name
.BR sprite .
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "Right button"
.TP
.B Left button
Paint with the selected palette colour.
.TP
.B Right button
Erase to transparency.
.TP
.B r/R, g/G, b/B
Decrease or increase the corresponding colour channel.
.TP
.B X
Select transparent ink.
.TP
.B S
Save the embedded block.
.TP
.B L
Reload it from disk.
.TP
.B N
Clear the sprite.
.TP
.B Tab
Cycle the mesh editing plane.
.TP
.B Q, Escape
Quit.
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/spriteedit.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR acme (1),
.IR plumb (1),
.IR wm (1)
